# Architecture migration session (Holzen)

**Incremental, behavior-preserving** alignment of active `src/` with documented architecture — not a big-bang rewrite. **Lovable:** Vite root stays at repo root; do **not** move SPA to `apps/web` or extract `packages/*` unless explicitly asked.

## Initiative scope vs scheduling priority

Two ideas — do not conflate them:

| | Meaning |
|---|---------|
| **Initiative scope (north star)** | Align **all active `src/`** — app, screens, components, features, lib ([client-architecture-overview.md](../../docs/fundamentals/client-architecture-overview.md)) — with P1–P9 and the shared module skeleton ([pause-client-architecture.md](../../docs/systems/pause-client-architecture.md) §9). |
| **Scheduling priority (what to do next)** | **Pause-first** at each slice tier: finish pause violations at the current tier before taking the same tier in another context — unless the user names a different target. |

**Pause is the reference implementation** (largest context). It is **not** the only domain on this branch. After pause is clean at a tier, apply the same slice pattern to subscription, auth, market, etc.

**Phases** (same branch): (0) client-architecture doc scaffolds → (A) pause convergence → (B) cross-context → (C) app/screens/lib hygiene. Backlog: [docs/artifacts/architecture-migration/README.md](../../docs/artifacts/architecture-migration/README.md).

